 is trained by adjusting the weights of the output layer only. Training involves exposing the reservoir to input data and then training a simple linear regressor on top of the reservoir's state to predict the desired output. Reservoirs are often trained using random weights to ensure they can capture a wide range of dynamics, making them efficient for tasks like anomaly detection.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":44884000,"total_duration":1448879400}}